// A stop delivered in a callee (a backwards interval, as in Card #2302)
// leaves through every caller's stop edge. Under SSA stress the stop points'
// Bools shared a slot with other values, so selection did not take their Ifs
// as stop edges: RNG.int returned without reporting its stop (edx 0), its
// caller went on, and the program ended in an internal error instead of the
// stop.
use core.math.random as random

fn run() {
    rng := random.rng(1)
    &rng.int(9, 3).drop("only the backwards-interval stop matters")
}
